  "content": {
    "id": "p50-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Given $x^3-2x^2+ax+6$ is divisible by $x-1$, find the value of $a$ and hence factorise the polynomial.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=-5$; $(x-1)(x+2)(x-3)$",
      "worked": "Let $P(x)=x^3-2x^2+ax+6$. Since $x-1$ is a factor, $P(1)=0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(1)&=1-2+a+6\\\\a+5&=0\\\\a&=-5\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $a=-5$ and divide by $x-1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}P(x)&=x^3-2x^2-5x+6\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x^2-x-6)\\\\P(x)&=(x-1)(x+2)(x-3).\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
